    <ul>
        <li>Compare the three ways to define a route, name the one this project uses, and defend it</li>
        <li>Explain why the route lives in a serialized list rather than in two hard-coded positions</li>
        <li>Point at the one field that is your enemy's whole memory of where it is going, and the line that changes it</li>
        <li>Explain what happens without the wrap, and name the exception it produces</li>
        <li>Say what <code>Vector3.MoveTowards()</code> refuses to do that a velocity line does, and why the third argument is <code>speed * Time.deltaTime</code></li>
        <li>Say how many enemies and how many coins the Overworld shipped with</li>
        <li>Commit and push</li>
    </ul>
</div>

